    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe de-duplication needed to combine two concerns that live in different places, so I split them accordingly:\n\n**1. Persistence check \u2014 `OwnerRepository`**\nAdded `existsByCustomerCode(String)` to the repository interface and its three implementations:\n- `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (the active `spring-data-jpa` profile) \u2014 Spring Data derives the query automatically.\n- `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 a `COUNT` JPQL query.\n- `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 a `COUNT(*) ... WHERE customer_code = :customerCode` query (the `customer_code` column exists in every schema).\n\n**2. Code-format / suffix logic \u2014 `CustomerCodeGenerator`**\nAdded a `deduplicate(String customerCode, Predicate<String> isTaken)` method. Since the generator already owns the *shape* of a customer code, the `'-<n>'` collision-suffix format (smallest `n \u2265 2` that is free) belongs here too. It stays pure \u2014 it takes a predicate rather than depending on persistence.\n\n**3. Orchestration \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`**\nGenerates the base code as before, then passes it through `deduplicate(..., ownerRepository::existsByCustomerCode)` before setting it on the owner and saving.\n\nThis keeps each unit single-purpose: the repository knows persistence, the generator knows code formatting/collision rules, and the service just wires the two together \u2014 no class became a catch-all.",
